{
  "$schema": "https://technocore.dev/schemas/composable-claim-graph/v1/policy-resolution.json",
  "id": "ex:recursive-trust-delegation-v1",
  "description": "Demonstrates a multi-hop trust delegation: a relying party accepts a claim iff it is signed by either the root authority OR any party the root has delegated trust to, recursively up to depth 3. Uses $ref chains rather than copying issuer lists, so delegation is composable and cache-friendly.",
  "policy": {
    "id": "policy:delegate-recursive",
    "issuer": "did:key:z6MkRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRoot",
    "validFrom": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
    "rules": [
      {
        "op": "or",
        "any": [
          {
            "op": "attest",
            "claim": "claim:root-is-issuer",
            "requireIssuer": "did:key:z6MkRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRoot"
          },
          {
            "op": "attest",
            "claim": "claim:delegation-grant",
            "requireIssuer": { "$ref": "did:key:z6MkRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRoot" },
            "constrain": {
              "subject": { "$ref": "#issuer" },
              "predicate": "canIssue",
              "value": true
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "resolver": {
    "maxDepth": 3,
    "cyclePolicy": "reject-on-cycle",
    "cache": {
      "strategy": "lru",
      "maxEntries": 1024,
      "ttlSeconds": 300,
      "key": "sha256(policyId + claimHash + issuerDid)"
    },
    "fetchHints": {
      "claim:root-is-issuer": "https://anchors.technocore.dev/root-attestation.json",
      "claim:delegation-grant": "https://anchors.technocore.dev/delegation/{issuer}.json"
    }
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "label": "direct root signature (depth 0)",
      "issuer": "did:key:z6MkRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRoot",
      "claim": { "id": "claim:root-is-issuer", "subject": "did:example:user123", "predicate": "kycVerified", "value": true },
      "expectedResult": { "allow": true, "depth": 0, "path": ["root"] }
    },
    {
      "label": "single-hop delegation (depth 1)",
      "issuer": "did:key:z6MkDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegate",
      "claim": { "id": "claim:delegation-grant", "subject": "did:example:user123", "predicate": "kycVerified", "value": true },
      "supporting": [
        {
          "issuer": "did:key:z6MkRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRoot",
          "claim": { "id": "claim:delegation-grant", "subject": "did:key:z6MkDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegate", "predicate": "canIssue", "value": true }
        }
      ],
      "expectedResult": { "allow": true, "depth": 1, "path": ["root", "delegate-1"] }
    },
    {
      "label": "two-hop delegation (depth 2)",
      "issuer": "did:key:z6MkDelegateTwoDelegateTwoDelegateTwo",
      "claim": { "id": "claim:delegation-grant", "subject": "did:example:user123", "predicate": "kycVerified", "value": true },
      "supporting": [
        {
          "issuer": "did:key:z6MkDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegate",
          "claim": { "id": "claim:delegation-grant", "subject": "did:key:z6MkDelegateTwoDelegateTwoDelegateTwo", "predicate": "canIssue", "value": true }
        },
        {
          "issuer": "did:key:z6MkRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRootAuthorityRoot",
          "claim": { "id": "claim:delegation-grant", "subject": "did:key:z6MkDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegateOneDelegate", "predicate": "canIssue", "value": true }
        }
      ],
      "expectedResult": { "allow": true, "depth": 2, "path": ["root", "delegate-1", "delegate-2"] }
    },
    {
      "label": "delegation beyond maxDepth must be rejected",
      "issuer": "did:key:z6MkDelegateFourDelegateFourDelegate",
      "claim": { "id": "claim:delegation-grant", "subject": "did:example:user123", "predicate": "kycVerified", "value": true },
      "supporting_chain_length": 4,
      "expectedResult": { "allow": false, "reason": "maxDepth exceeded (got 4, limit 3)" }
    },
    {
      "label": "cycle in delegation must be rejected",
      "graph": {
        "A": ["B"],
        "B": ["C"],
        "C": ["A"]
      },
      "expectedResult": { "allow": false, "reason": "cycle detected: A -> B -> C -> A", "detector": "patterns/claim-graph-resolver/src/cycle-detector.ts" }
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The $ref on requireIssuer lets the resolver pin the signer to whichever DID ended up being the issuer of the supporting claim — this is what makes delegation traversal work without enumerating delegates inline.",
    "Depth is measured as supporting-claim hops from the root, not as JSON nesting, so the cap is intuitive for operators.",
    "Combine with patterns/composable-claim-graph/examples/cycle-detection-policy.json to see how cycles are short-circuited before depth is consumed."
  ]
}

